Hello everybody,

I am wondering what could cause my model fail to calculate deterministic nodes.
My model has successfully run before. I've only updated the likelihood functions using new covariates (matrix) instead of old covariates (vector) then suddenly all  f_ne and mu nodes values are NA.
The warning message is "value of deterministic node: value is NA or NaN even after trying to calculate"
I have checked and all the covariates have no missing value. For the initial values, I've used the results from the analysis with another package.
I included the likelihood specification below, all the dimensions have been checked.

Thank you very much.
Hannah.

## Likelihood
    for (i in 1:nUnits){
    for(j in 1:(nTime-max_lag)){
      tY[i,j] ~ dnegbin(p[i,j],r)
      p[i,j] <- r/(r+mu[i,j])
      mu[i,j] <- f_ne[i,j]*neY[i,j]

        log(f_ne[i,j]) <- beta.n[1] + beta.n[2]*weekend2[j,i] +
        beta.n[3]*travelmat.centered[j,i] + beta.n[4]*travelmat2.centered[j,i] +
        beta.n[5]*str.mat[j,i] + beta.n[6]*logpop_std[j,i]
    }
  }

