hi Brook,

This is a bit puzzling as:
1) We don't have anything in how we configure compilation that would add the "-R" flag
2) Your output shows "path/to/lib", which seems like something inserted generically. I presume your machine does not actually have such a directory structure.

Do you have your own Makevars file (either in your home directory or in the directory used as the current working directory by R)? If so, values set in there might be affecting things. Or perhaps somehow values in a Makeconf file somewhere might be messing things up. We have a bit of info about this in Section 4.5.4 of the user manual. <http://Note%20that%20you%20can't%20have%20a%20space%20after%20the%20initial%20$%20for%20the%20inline%20equations.> You might look in /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/etc.

You might also check the nimble/CppCode/Makevars and nimble/make/Makevars files in your installed nimble directory to see if those might have been messed up somehow.

-chris

